[{"id":68962,"sender_id":639,"sender_full_name":"Praphulla Koushik","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/4d3ba0c0a767b7329e0f56993aceb259?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Definition.20of.20Lie.20groupoid.20extension/near/68962\">#1</a> I am having difficulty understanding definition of Lie groupoid extension as in https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0511696v5</p>\n<p>NLab page https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/centrally+extended+groupoid is also not easy to understand.</p>\n<p>Can some one tell me what should be a reasonable definition of Lie groupoid extension.</p>","timestamp":1530985219,"subject":"Definition of Lie groupoid extension","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":68964,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Definition.20of.20Lie.20groupoid.20extension/near/68964\">#2</a> The abstract idea is extremely simple: Given your Lie groupoid <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7805em;vertical-align:-0.0972em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathcal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0593em;\">G</span></span></span></span>, regard it as  <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/smooth%20stack\">smooth stack</a> and consider a morphism of smooth stacks of the form</p>\n<p><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">G</mi><mo>⟶</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\n  \\mathcal{G} \\longrightarrow \\mathbf{B}^2 U(1)\n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7805em;vertical-align:-0.0972em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathcal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0593em;\">G</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">⟶</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.1141em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">B</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8641em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">U</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span></span></p>\n<p>to the <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/circle%203-group\">circle 3-group</a>. Then the <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/homotopy%20fiber\">homotopy fiber</a> of this morphism is a Lie groupoid central extension <span class=\"tex-error\">$\\widehat \\mathcal{G}$</span>, and, conversely every central extension arises this way, up to equivalence</p>\n<p><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mtable rowspacing=\"0.16em\" columnalign=\"center center center\" columnspacing=\"1em\"><mtr><mtd><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">G</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\">^</mo></mover></mstyle></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">↓</mo></mstyle></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">G</mi></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">⟶</mo></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\n  \\begin{matrix}\n   \\widehat{\\mathcal{G}}\n    \\\\\n    \\downarrow\n    \\\\\n    \\mathcal{G} &amp;\\longrightarrow&amp; \\mathbf{B}^2 U(1)\n  \\end{matrix}\n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:3.6833em;vertical-align:-1.5917em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.0917em;\"><span style=\"top:-4.1683em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9233em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathcal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0593em;\">G</span></span><span class=\"svg-align\" style=\"width:calc(100% - 0.2222em);margin-left:0.2222em;top:-3.6833em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span style=\"height:0.24em;\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"100%\" height=\"0.24em\" viewBox=\"0 0 1062 239\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"><path d=\"M529 0h5l519 115c5 1 9 5 9 10 0 1-1 2-1 3l-4 22\nc-1 5-5 9-11 9h-2L532 67 19 159h-2c-5 0-9-4-11-9l-5-22c-1-6 2-12 8-13z\"/></svg></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.0972em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.9683em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mrel\">↓</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.7683em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathcal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0593em;\">G</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.5917em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:-0.3917em;\"><span style=\"top:-1.7683em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mrel\">⟶</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.5917em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:-0.3917em;\"><span style=\"top:-1.7683em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">B</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">U</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.5917em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n<p>That’s all there is. The real question now is with which set of generators and relations for <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/smooth%20stacks\">smooth stacks</a> you would like to work. Depending on this choice, this simple idea can take any number of incarnations, and makes for many publications and PhD theses ;-)</p>","timestamp":1530986377,"subject":"Definition of Lie groupoid extension","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":68965,"sender_id":639,"sender_full_name":"Praphulla Koushik","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/4d3ba0c0a767b7329e0f56993aceb259?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Definition.20of.20Lie.20groupoid.20extension/near/68965\">#3</a> I understand what does it mean to say see a Lie groupoid as a smooth stack.. it is denoted by <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"script\">G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B\\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7805em;vertical-align:-0.0972em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mord mathcal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0593em;\">G</span></span></span></span> in some papers, it is a category whose objects are Principal <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7805em;vertical-align:-0.0972em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathcal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0593em;\">G</span></span></span></span> bundles and morphisms are <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7805em;vertical-align:-0.0972em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathcal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0593em;\">G</span></span></span></span> invariant morphisms… I believe this is what you mean when you say smooth stack associated to Lie groupoid… it is actually written as <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"script\">G</mi><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B\\mathcal{G}\\rightarrow {\\mathrm{Man}}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7805em;vertical-align:-0.0972em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mord mathcal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0593em;\">G</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Man</span></span></span></span></span></span>.. I know what is a morphism of stack but I do not know about this particular stack <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B^2 U(1)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">U</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> you have written… Then you are saying(not defining) homotopy fiber of this morphism of Lie groupoids is a Lie groupoid central xtnsion.. And you are saying any Lie groupoid central extension has to come like this.. </p>\n<p>Can you say what is a Lie groupoid central extension, I mean the definition… I have to understand only Lie groupoid extensions but I am also open for understanding some special kind of Lie groupoid extensions I.e., Lie groupoid central extensions (I guess Lie groupoid central extensions as you said are special case of Lie groupoid extensions)</p>\n<p>Thank you and yes I am looking for some problem for my PhD thesis :) :)</p>","timestamp":1530987555,"subject":"Definition of Lie groupoid extension","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":68968,"sender_id":43,"sender_full_name":"DavidRoberts","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fbc2dbfb28f9e9275a4fd4cd109b5a21?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Definition.20of.20Lie.20groupoid.20extension/near/68968\">#4</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>makes for many publications and PhD theses ;-)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>surely that’s not cynical sarcasm?! :-o</p>","timestamp":1531038631,"subject":"Definition of Lie groupoid extension","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":68972,"sender_id":639,"sender_full_name":"Praphulla Koushik","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/4d3ba0c0a767b7329e0f56993aceb259?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Definition.20of.20Lie.20groupoid.20extension/near/68972\">#5</a> https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/0511696.pdf in page 5 they define what is a Lie groupoid extension.</p>\n<p>Let <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⇉</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X_1\\rightrightarrows M</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8641em;vertical-align:-0.1808em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0785em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel amsrm\">⇉</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⇉</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X_2\\rightrightarrows M</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8641em;vertical-align:-0.1808em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0785em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel amsrm\">⇉</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span></span></span></span> be two Lie groupoids. </p>\n<p>A Lie groupoid extension is a morphism of Lie groupoids <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"kat